  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Browser-native 3D DICOM viewer from Kitware (VTK/ITK/ParaView lineage) with a clear differentiator: cinematic volume rendering running entirely client-side with no data upload, no installation, and no server dependency. NIH-funded, MICCAI 2022 paper, v4.4.0, Apache-2.0. Assess rather than Adopt: 283 stars and DICOM-only format support (no NIfTI/NRRD), which limits it to radiology workflows vs. broader neuroimaging use cases covered by NiiVue or 3D Slicer (both already in MACH). The zero-install local-processing model is a strong fit for privacy-sensitive clinical environments. Adopt OHIF Viewer for full-featured DICOM worklist and annotation; Assess VolView for lightweight 3D rendering without infrastructure.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-04",
